 "description": "Read an online store's products, prices and availability, and what changed since its previous daily snapshot. Use it for questions like \"track competitor prices on allbirds.com\", \"what did gymshark.com change?\", \"what is new or sold out at this store?\". Pass store addresses, up to 5: a bare host such as \"allbirds.com\", an https link to any page of the store, or a myshopify.com address. Works only for Shopify stores that publish their public product feed (/products.json). Calling it adds the store to a daily snapshot list, so its history builds up. Optional: query (text in a product's title, brand, type or handle), limit. Returns per store a status, the snapshot date, product count, currency, change counts and lists of new, removed, repriced and restocked or sold-out variants, plus matching products. The first snapshot has no changes. Not for one product's history (use get_product_price_history) or for comparing two stores (use compare_store_prices).",
 "inputSchema": {
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
   "limit": {
    "description": "Most products listed per section (default 10)",
    "maximum": 25,
    "minimum": 1,
    "type": "integer"
   },
   "query": {
    "description": "Only products whose title, brand, type or handle contains this text, such as \"hoodie\"",
    "maxLength": 200,
    "type": "string"
   },
   "stores": {
    "description": "Store web addresses, up to 5, such as [\"allbirds.com\"]. Each one may be a bare host (\"gymshark.com\"), an https link to any page of the store, or a myshopify.com address.",
    "items": {
     "maxLength": 300,
     "minLength": 1,
     "type": "string"
    },
    "maxItems": 5,
    "minItems": 1,
    "type": "array"
   }
  },
  "required": [
   "stores"
  ],
  "type": "object"
 },
